# Pinned counts for scripts/gate_published_consistency.sh — a RATCHET, not a pass mark.
#
# These are KNOWN-OPEN defects, not acceptable ones. The gate fails if a count RISES, and tells you
# to tighten the pin if a count FALLS. The point is that a published-consistency defect can no longer
# be introduced silently; the standing ones stay visible instead of being waved through by a gate
# that prints FAIL on every push and is therefore read by nobody.
#
# Recorded 2026-09-06. Re-pin in the SAME commit as any change that legitimately moves a count.
#
# G1 — unfilled placeholders in published reports.
#      5: [REPRO-TAG] x2 (a git tag minted at TR-12 publication; it cannot be filled before the
#      freeze) and [EXPECTED-Q1|Q9|XA] x3 (filled by the n=31 battery's expected-output blocks,
#      which do not exist until that run happens).
G1=5
# G2 — published --estimate-knuth commands with no thread pin.
#      10: NOT fixable by adding a number. Measured 2026-09-06: 45 files under reports/evidence/
#      carry a threads= header, so the counts exist, but the mapping from a PUBLISHED FIGURE to the
#      RUN that produced it is not recorded. TR7_CIRCULAR_READING.md:158 has six candidate evidence
#      files matching its probe count and nothing says which one produced the published figures.
#      Adding a pin would FABRICATE provenance, which is worse than the gap. The real defect is one
#      level up: a published command does not name the artifact it reproduces.
G2=10
# G3 — published disclosures that have gone stale. Shaped to fire when the artifact EXISTS.
G3=0
# G4 — corrections that name a propagation target which does not carry the correction id.
#      8: CX-28 (documentation/README.md, reports/README.md, TR4) and CX-33 (SPECIFICATION,
#      SYMMETRY_SEARCH, TRIGRAM_STRUCTURE, lean/README, METHODS). Pre-existing, found the day this
#      gate was written. Each needs an editorial decision -- whether the correction genuinely applies
#      to that file, or whether the Documents list overreached -- so they are pinned, not bulk-edited.
G4=8
# G5 — LEADERBOARD's edit-distance table vs section [28] of the artifact it cites. Fixed 2026-09-07.
G5=0
# G6 — per-cell tree sizes labelled canonical above the 28! ceiling. Fixed 2026-09-07.
G6=0
# G7 — the per-position entropy table vs section [2] of the artifact it cites. Fixed 2026-09-07.
G7=0
# G8 — a fixed constrained-position range asserted across all datasets. Fixed 2026-09-07.
G8=0
# G9 — published --branch recipes without a budget; --validate naming a phantom path. Fixed 2026-09-07.
G9=0
# G10 — a TR revision row that re-scopes or withdraws, with no corrections-ledger entry naming both
#       that TR and that date. This is the class G4 is STRUCTURALLY BLIND to: G4 walks the 35 "## CX-"
#       entries, so a correction recorded only in a TR's revision table is outside its universe and
#       G4 reports PASS by construction. Measured on the day this leg was written: TR-8 v1.16
#       (2026-08-30) re-scoped its Gray-code theorem and CLAIMS_DECIDED still graded the claim
#       REFUTED (proven) seven days later.
#       1: TR3 v1.11 (2026-08-31), "eight corrections from the executed prose review (batch P09)".
#       Pinned rather than bulk-edited because whether a batch of eight prose corrections warrants a
#       ledger entry is an editorial call, not a mechanical one.
G10=1
# G11 — a published gain series must name the boundary the archived run picked. Fixed 2026-09-07.
G11=0
# G12 — a pre-registered gate must be quoted with its own threshold. Fixed 2026-09-07.
G12=0
# G13 — the forced-exception claim vs the fiber sweep. Fixed 2026-09-07.
G13=0
# G14 — a boundary-count projection must record the oriented-fiber floor. Fixed 2026-09-07.
G14=0
# G15 — a DATA-LIKE registry row must not be counted as source-stated. Fixed 2026-09-07.
G15=0
